{"title":"What should I ask Theodore H. Schwartz?","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/911046875/0/marginalrevolution~What-should-I-ask-Theodore-H-Schwartz.html","date":1736959406000,"content":"<p>Yes I will be doing a Conversation with him.  He is a famous brain surgeon and author of the recent and excellent book <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Gray-Matters-Biography-Brain-Surgery/dp/0593474104/ref=sr_1_1?crid=VCXQ9491Z03T&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.LMWQ6wL_0dJ7nk8_9oqrhS9qRMBKKCvAt9nZIt6rw3jChNUSIRPxZV1iiYph-gKqg2VU0MCF7nQ3cLbH8USEcWeEA8nLUID8clYOs0Q44PwKhAlAkJZc8B9NdTy6Snz_e5Zc0uXvnwZChoZVcC4uhJpZDgwDrbRfIWf5l37dW4Fo7SoRO51HXpd_lj7ND8UagDM54M0O416FTSbe9hPG1IYhXPjN_eWYf4zS4GxCrT4.RwNa-Ycz-TXEDmw0vgzANVYd7rToP4vWXveAf6blN3E&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=brain+surgery+history&amp;qid=1736908763&amp;s=books&amp;sprefix=brain+surgery+history%2Cstripbooks%2C82&amp;sr=1-1\" target=\"_blank\">Gray Matters: A Biography of Brain Surgery</a>.</p>\r\n<p>Here is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodore_H._Schwartz\" target=\"_blank\">his Wikipedia page</a>, and an opening excerpt:</p>\r\n<blockquote><p><b>Theodore H. Schwartz</b> (born May 13, 1965) is an American <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medical\">medical</a> scientist, academic <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Physician\">physician</a> and <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neurosurgeon\">neurosurgeon</a>.</p>\r\n<p>Schwartz specializes in surgery for <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brain_tumors\">brain tumors</a>, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pituitary_tumors\">pituitary tumors</a> and <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Epilepsy\">epilepsy</a>. He is particularly known for developing and expanding the field of minimally-invasive endonasal endoscopic <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skull_base\">skull base</a> and pituitary surgery and for his research on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neurovascular_coupling\">neurovascular coupling</a> and propagation of epilepsy.</p></blockquote>\r\n<p>Here is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.theodorehschwartzmd.com/\" target=\"_blank\">his home page</a>.  So what should I ask him?</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/01/what-should-i-ask-theodore-h-schwartz.html\">What should I ask Theodore H. Schwartz?</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/911046875/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/911046875/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/911046875/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/24/911046875/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/x.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/19/911046875/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/email20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/20/911046875/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/rs